   "title": "No net knock-down on CLmax",
   "text": "Design CLmax = 1.0 x the critical-section CLmax built on the XFOIL clmax envelope",
   "basis": "XFOIL tends to over-predict clmax at Re 2-3e5 by a few per cent, while the critical-section method under-predicts a low-AR rectangular wing (stall spreads before CL peaks) and the clmax envelope is already the lower of Re 2.3e5 / 3.0e5; the biases offset. Replaced by the slow-flight stall T-B2-STALL",
   "value": 1.0,
   "unit": "-",
