   "state": "planned",
   "procedure": "A foot (shoe bonded on a 2-layer foam-board offcut clamped vertical) under a 0.65 kg sled on two guide rods; free drop 0.115 m onto plywood; phone or logger accelerometer on the sled. 3 drops, new cartridge each. Pass: stroke <= 29 mm, sled peak <= 6.0 g (100 Hz filter), no shoe-bond crack. With the biased, pre-crushed cartridges (CR-C5-10, R3) use a 0.68 kg sled for an upper-foot cartridge and 0.62 kg for a lower one (quarter gate mass x bias). Run before the aircraft drop; cheap and repeatable.",
